# BUG-242 regression fixture — the whole Csv namespace was dead in the selfhost.
#
# Pins the two halves separately, because they failed for different reasons and the
# original ticket only knew about the second:
#   READER  — the preamble's parser still reassigned `.{}` to unmanaged ArrayLists after
#             the Zig 0.16 migration, so `Csv.parse` did not compile at all.
#   WRITER  — the selfhost emitted `CsvWriter()` verbatim into Zig (no constructor), and
#             once that worked, `build()` was typed as a raw slice rather than str, so it
#             printed `{ 97, 44, 98 }` instead of text. That one compiled CLEANLY — valid
#             Zig producing wrong output — so only running it can catch a return.
def main()
    var t = Csv.parse("name,city\nAlice,Boston")
    assert t.rowCount() == 2, "reader: rowCount"
    assert t.colCount() == 2, "reader: colCount"

    var h = t.header()
    assert h.at(0) == "name", "reader: header cell"

    var r = t.row(1)
    assert t.get(r, "city") == "Boston", "reader: lookup by column name"

    var w = CsvWriter()
    w.writeRow(h)
    w.writeRow(r)
    var out = w.build()

    # If build() regresses to a byte array these fail, which is the whole point.
    assert out.contains("name,city"), "writer: header text, not bytes"
    assert out.contains("Alice"), "writer: data row text, not bytes"

    print("bug242: OK")
